<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Domini di Terraferma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1339–1797</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Venetian Terraferma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Domini di Terraferma were the mainland territories of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, conquered mainly between 1339 and 1428 and including Treviso, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicenza">Vicenza</a>, Verona, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brescia">Brescia</a> and Bergamo, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a>. They kept their own statutes and councils under Venetian governors. Lost almost entirely after Agnadello in 1509, they were mostly recovered by 1517 and held until 1797.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/domini-di-terraferma.jpg" alt="Domini di Terraferma" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utente:-kayac- · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Repubblica_Venezia_espansione_in_Terraferma.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
